1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,700
This is the story of little Runa Sasaki, a young girl with an overprotective mother and a father with a gentle heart.

2
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:19,440
Thanks to them and her older brother, who's always a step ahead and looking after her, Miss Runa was brought up in this world like a princess.

3
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:29,840
Some of the things she loves are the chocolate donuts from the venerable neighborhood donut shop, the online games she excels at.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,760
And especially her gamer friends who always treat her so kindly.

5
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:45,920
As for unfamiliar places, unfamiliar things, and unfamiliar people, she hates them.

6
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Growing up, little Runa Sasaki was a coddled child.

7
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:30,000
As a result, she believes if she keeps quiet and puts on airs, someone is bound to show her kindness.

8
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
But this sets Runa apart from her classmates who don't really know what to make of her.

9
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
At times, she was the target of bullying from the older students.

10
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,000
However, since she has 300 friends online, this never really bothered her.

11
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Even if the girls who'd been her classmates for all three years were...

12
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Miss Sasaki, you're on duty today, right?

13
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Are you going to clear the blackboard?

14
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Oh, right. Still calling her by her last name?

15
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
It doesn't really bother Runa.

16
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:11,000
By the way, little Runa Sasaki was born blessed with breathtakingly pretty features.

17
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,000
So many of the boys in her grade have developed a secret crush on her.

18
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:22,000
But as her casual attire, which she can be seen wearing on school trips, is of the hardcore Lolita variety,

19
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:28,000
and since her hair color is slightly different than the other girls, the boys end up keeping their distance from her.

20
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:36,000
On top of that, Runa's older brother is charmingly handsome, and this friend who she's known since childhood is a knockout.

21
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:40,000
In her eyes, they've become the standard for all guys.

22
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Which means that the boys in her class all look like this to her.

23
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Hey, look you guys! I recorded a new video!

24
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Aw, that's so adorable!

25
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
I was dancing with you, Kachi!

26
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
You tried too!

27
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Just watch!

28
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
First you go like this, and…

29
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
What are those moves?

30
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Oh no, I'm gonna be late!

31
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Ah-chan, Makolin, see you!

32
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Yeah, later, Lee-chan!

33
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Bye-bye!

34
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Uh, see you later too, Miss Sasaki!

35
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Good luck!

36
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,000
You bet!

37
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,000
But the truth about little Runa Sasaki…

38
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Bye-bye…

39
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Is that she's a lion at home and a mouse outside, spoiled and cowardly.

40
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Coming!

41
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Recently, though, Runa met someone new.

42
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Hey, Runa, you made it!

43
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:52,000
And became friends with a girl who's a bit older than her.

44
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
I got you some of that new pudding from the convenience store!

45
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Since Akane is a little more grown up than the other girls in Runa's class…

46
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Akane!

47
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
I saw this weird dance at school today.

48
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Oh yeah? You wanna show me?

49
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:10,000
She's always nice to Runa, even when she can be mean or acts like a spoiled child.

50
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Because of this, Runa is somewhat aware that even though they're friends now,

51
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
they're not exactly on equal footing.

52
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Oh yeah, and you know what else?

53
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Hey, hold up a sec.

54
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
My friend just sent me something.

55
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
But since Akane is neither family nor a childhood friend…

56
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
It's not like she's going to act the way Runa wants her to.

57
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Who is this other friend?

58
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Respond to them later!

59
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
They're with Runa right now!

60
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:41,000
And it's not like she'll take the time to comfort her when she gets pouty and sulky either.

61
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Actually, she doesn't even notice her sulking.

62
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Ugh! Runa! Check this out!

63
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
They're shooting a TV show in front of the station!

64
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
And that super hot actor Sato is there!

65
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
You wanna go see?

66
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
I didn't know you were such a big fangirl, Akane.

67
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
I sure am! Are you with me?

68
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
But…

69
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Come on, hurry, hurry!

70
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Just wait a minute!

71
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:04,000
It's a little different than when she's with her brother and friends!

72
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
There's a new kind of excitement!

73
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Even though she supposedly doesn't like unfamiliar things or unfamiliar people!

74
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Even from far away, Sato really is so dreamy!

75
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,000
You really think so?

76
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Yamada's way better looking though!

77
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Sure he is, but Yamada's Yamada, you know?

78
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Yeah, that's true…

79
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Oh, hey! Check out those people over there!

80
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
They're dancing! Doesn't that look fun?

81
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Runa doesn't understand why anyone would dance in the street.

82
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:43,000
I don't know, don't you wanna jump in with that weird dance you showed me?

83
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Not in your life!

84
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Was it like this?

85
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
No, like this!

86
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
But here lately…

87
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:57,000
She's beginning to think that it could actually be fun if she made more friends who'd do this weird dance with her.

88
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Just a tiny bit.

89
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:07,000
I really want to fall in love.

90
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:16,000
According to the life plan I put together, I'm supposed to be getting married as soon as I graduate from college.

91
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:23,000
My mom had me when she was in her early twenties, so to be like her, I've always wanted to get married as young as possible.

92
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:27,000
But before that can even happen, I'd need to find myself a husband, right?

93
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
And to lock down a husband by then, I need a boyfriend first, don't I?

94
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
That's why more than anything, I really want to fall in love…

95
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Uh, wait a sec. You should let the attacker finish it off.

96
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Right. Now you're almost there.

97
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
I did it! The quest is cleared!

98
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Neither of you nerds heard a single word I just said, did you?

99
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Oh, sorry. Check it out, Momo.

100
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
I've managed to reach level 50 in just a week, isn't that so…

101
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Not interested. Keep following Runa's instructions and you can max out your level by the end of the month.

102
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Akane.

103
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:04,000
This is your precious free day. Are you sure you should be binging on an online game with a runaway middle school kid?

104
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Oh, she's not a runaway. She had an argument with her brother, so it's awkward for her at home, you know?

105
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Fine, but she's still a child. I mean, what does playing online games with her say about the two of us?

106
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:19,000
If this is boring you so badly, why don't you just go home? You didn't have a good reason for coming here anyway.

107
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Quiet, you.

108
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Don't mess with me, little girl.

109
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:30,000
You don't know how lucky you are, Akane. Wish I could meet a handsome young guy.

110
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Do you mean Yamada? Trust me, it isn't like that, okay?

111
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Although we have gotten a little closer lately, and he let me add him to my friends list.

112
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:43,000
But he's as surly as ever, and he still won't go hunting with me either.

113
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Well, that's because your levels are too far apart, and it wouldn't be very profitable for him.

114
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:54,000
But whenever I ask him about equipment, he gives me all kinds of advice. He's actually surprisingly helpful.

115
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Really? As long as I've known him, Yamada's never been anything but helpful.

116
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Even though he's studying for his own entrance exams, he still comes to tutor Runa, too.

117
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Huh? He must be super popular.

118
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Yeah, he was beyond popular, but I've never seen him with a girlfriend, so he must be pretty awkward with girls.

119
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:15,000
What? That's such a waste! Maybe I'll volunteer for the job.

120
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Hmm? Speak of the devil.

121
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Speak of the devil.

122
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Hey there! Yamada!

123
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Hey.

124
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
It sure has been a while since I've seen you online.

125
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:34,000
I guess so. I've been busy lately.

126
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Hey, listen! I finally got my shoes all upgraded, like you taught me the other day!

127
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Hmm.

128
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
It is? But I was supposed to use int gems like you, wasn't I?

129
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I thought I did it just how you showed me.

130
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
I use ints because I'm playing a wizard, but a paladin should be using vits.

131
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Huh? Then I can't use these gems?

132
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
But I worked so hard to collect them, too.

133
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Do you want to use my spare pair of shoes?

134
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
I have a set that's been fully upgraded for tank classes.

135
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Hmm.

136
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Hmm.

137
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
It's okay.

138
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
I just have to collect those vip things, right?

139
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
In that case, I'm gonna go hunting again to collect them.

140
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
It'll be easy now that I know where they drop.

141
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Yeah, of course. Sorry about that. I was out of line.

142
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Good luck with your upgrades.

143
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:40,000
A smiley-faced emote? That never happens!

144
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Now she's screaming to herself. Is she finally having a breakdown?

145
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
She's having fun.

146
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:54,000
This is so boring! All you've done today is play that game! I want to go outside or go on a group date or something!

147
00:10:55,000 --> 00:11:01,000
You want to give it a try, Momo? It's actually pretty fun.

148
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
You know games aren't my thing!

149
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
Oh, come on! Just try it out!

150
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
But I'm clueless when it comes to computers!

151
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Once you get the hang of it, they're easy to operate!

152
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Here, look. I'm going on a hunt now, so watch me!

153
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:34,000
I don't know the first thing about computers and stuff, but it's a bad sign if there's smoke coming out, right?

154
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Akanechi's computer had a breakdown?

155
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Yeah, it exploded in her face while she was playing boss.

156
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
Makes sense. The last update really puts a strain on outdated hardware.

157
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
I guess her system couldn't handle it.

158
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:55,000
She says she won't be able to play again until she saves up enough for a new one.

159
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Seemed like it made her really sad.

160
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Coming!

161
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Who is it?

162
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Hello.

163
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
I heard you're in need of a repairman, so...

164
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Ta-da!

165
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,000
I can remember.

166
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:33,000
I remember.

167
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
I'll run away.

168
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Part Goodbye.

169
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Take one.

170
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,000
My name is Olaus אנis.

171
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Him.

172
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
I am.

173
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
I'm not.

174
00:12:48,000 --> 00:13:13,660
Yes?

175
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:15,140
Good morning, Yamada.

176
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:22,220
Hey, what's going on?

177
00:13:22,220 --> 00:13:24,720
By chance, you don't have a used computer, do you?

178
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:26,220
Like an old spare?

179
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:28,220
No, I don't.

180
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:33,980
The little birdie told me that Akanechi's computer broke down.

181
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:36,380
Apparently it was smoking and everything.

182
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:38,380
There was smoke?

183
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:40,100
Coming from where?

184
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:44,260
I haven't seen it myself, so I don't know.

185
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:48,540
So, do you think you could take a look at Akanechi's computer when you have time?

186
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:49,540
Me?

187
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:52,980
You might be able to fix it by just swapping out a part.

188
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:55,660
Wouldn't it be better if you went, Eita?

189
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:57,620
I mean, I wouldn't mind going.

190
00:13:57,620 --> 00:14:00,220
But what if there was some sort of misunderstanding?

191
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:04,340
You know, how would it look with a healthy guy going into a sweet college girl's apartment?

192
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:05,740
That seems risky.

193
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:08,020
What kind of guy do you think I am?

194
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:11,020
A new breed.

195
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:14,460
Runa mentioned that she was really depressed about it.

196
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:19,460
Akanechi's been grinding really hard and fast lately, so I feel bad for her.

197
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:23,300
Stop by after Runa's tutoring session, will ya?

198
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:26,260
I'll have Runa take you over to her apartment when you're done.

199
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:26,860
Okay?

200
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:28,540
Pretty please?

201
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:32,460
Mm-mm.

202
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:33,860
It's okay.

203
00:14:33,860 --> 00:14:36,700
I just have to collect those vid things, right?

204
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:40,460
In that case, I'm going to go hunting again to collect them.

205
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:50,940
You came to fix my computer, Yamada?

206
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:55,260
Yeah, and Runa's the one who brought him over!

207
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:56,860
I'm only here to take a look.

208
00:14:56,860 --> 00:14:58,460
Please don't get your hopes up.

209
00:14:58,460 --> 00:14:59,500
Runa did!

210
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:01,420
Oh, don't look at me like that.

211
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:04,060
Seriously, I don't even know if I can fix it yet.

212
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:04,620
Runa!

213
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:07,260
So it's a laptop.

214
00:15:07,260 --> 00:15:09,900
Feel free to make yourselves at home, okay?

215
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,580
Do either of you want some snacks?

216
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:12,460
Please, don't trouble.

217
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:13,020
I do!

218
00:15:14,060 --> 00:15:15,820
Yamada is such a good person!

219
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:17,820
Akane, Akane!

220
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:23,900
So, uh, hanging up in your room there, are those...

221
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:24,940
Okay?

222
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:34,780
Thank goodness, he didn't notice.

223
00:15:35,420 --> 00:15:37,820
Well, it's Yamada, so he wouldn't care anyway.

224
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:43,740
It does feel a little strange having Yamada in the house, but remember what Runa said.

225
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:45,100
He's awkward with girls.

226
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:49,340
I shouldn't be too self-conscious around him, or he'll get uncomfortable.

227
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:51,500
Just be me.

228
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:54,540
Hey, have the two of you eaten anything yet today?

229
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:57,660
If you haven't, I wouldn't mind whipping something up.

230
00:15:57,660 --> 00:15:58,780
I can eat!

231
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:00,540
What do you say, Yamada?

232
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:01,180
You want something?

233
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:05,820
Yes, I would like some.

234
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:08,060
Well, well, how rare!

235
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:09,580
No thanks.

236
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:12,940
I forgot to tell you this before.

237
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:13,740
Hmm?

238
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:19,020
That curry you gave me, it was really tasty.

239
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:23,820
Sorry, I just remembered, so I forgot to bring back your containers.

240
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:26,940
I'm glad!

241
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:31,900
I'll pour my heart and soul into making lunch, so eat up, okay?

242
00:16:36,940 --> 00:16:37,820
Hey, so listen.

243
00:16:38,540 --> 00:16:40,540
There's a new girl who's going to be joining our guild.

244
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:40,940
Huh?

245
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:44,460
She's a really sweet-natured girl, and she's just so cute!

246
00:16:45,100 --> 00:16:45,900
Kurihime!

247
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:49,420
The stranger yelled at me at the dungeon again!

248
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:51,740
I'm against bullying noobies!

249
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:55,260
One thing's for certain, she totally wears her heart on her sleeve.

250
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:57,580
Or should I say, she doesn't really hide who she is.

251
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:03,900
Yeah, a straightforward girl like her would be a good match for you, Akito.

252
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:06,940
I refuse to accept a stranger like that!

253
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:08,780
Who are you supposed to be, a sister-in-law?

254
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:19,340
I'm not interested.

255
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:23,900
It looks like the adapter pin's completely melted.

256
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:28,220
When did you buy this laptop?

257
00:17:28,220 --> 00:17:38,940
Well, it was back when I started college, so I would say...

258
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:42,700
It's happening!

259
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:56,700
Love comedy.

260
00:17:57,420 --> 00:17:58,060
Would that be...

261
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:03,420
Like this?

262
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:09,100
You've never cleaned your keyboard once, have you?

263
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:11,260
I didn't know you were supposed to!

264
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:12,620
There are traces of a spill.

265
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:13,500
No, stop!

266
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:14,540
Don't look close!

267
00:18:14,540 --> 00:18:28,140
We sure are having another lovely day!

268
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:37,100
Akane?

269
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:39,900
What's up?

270
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:41,660
Lunch is almost ready.

271
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:45,660
I was wondering, do you have plans to take a bath anytime soon?

272
00:18:46,540 --> 00:18:47,580
Not especially.

273
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:51,180
I'm cooking right now, so I'll be taking a bath later tonight.

274
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:58,140
Yamada, are you going to take a bath?

275
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,260
No, I'm not.

276
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:03,820
I don't really get it, so whatever.

277
00:19:04,860 --> 00:19:06,940
Akane, can I have a slice of bread, please?

278
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:08,220
Be my guest.

279
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,980
Aren't you going to get full eating all that before this?

280
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:13,980
I'm making all my rice now.

281
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:16,860
Don't worry, I'm not the one who'll be eating it.

282
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:17,420
What?

283
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:18,140
Oh!

284
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:30,220
Why did you eat it all?

285
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:31,980
Why did you make me eat it?

286
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:33,740
Hey, come over here for a sec!

287
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:34,460
Hold on!

288
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:37,260
You've got to get a little bit closer or there won't be a lucky birth moment!

289
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:38,140
It's dangerous!

290
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:40,300
What do you mean?

291
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:48,540
Huh, now what am I supposed to do?

292
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:49,340
Hey!

293
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:51,340
You need to stop right now!

294
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:52,860
Ouch!

295
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:54,860
Yamada, what's wrong?

296
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:57,580
Your hair hit my eyeball.

297
00:19:57,580 --> 00:19:58,380
No way!

298
00:19:58,380 --> 00:19:59,340
Sorry!

299
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:00,380
Are you okay?

300
00:20:00,380 --> 00:20:01,020
How's your eye?

301
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:04,140
Let me see it.

302
00:20:07,260 --> 00:20:07,740
Which eye?

303
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:21,500
I'm fine.

304
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:27,340
Oh crap!

305
00:20:27,340 --> 00:20:29,420
I panicked and grabbed his face without thinking!

306
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:31,660
I wonder if stuff like that really bothers him or something!

307
00:20:32,460 --> 00:20:34,220
I am so sorry, Yamada!

308
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:36,060
Come on, I'm gonna make you apologize too!

309
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:37,980
I'm sorry!

310
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:41,420
I'll tie my hair up, okay?

311
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:43,180
Yes?

312
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:46,300
Excuse me, I'm heading back home for a bit.

313
00:20:47,740 --> 00:20:50,140
I didn't bring over any of the tools I need, so...

314
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:52,140
Oh, but...

315
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:52,940
I'll be right back.

316
00:20:53,740 --> 00:20:55,340
Wait, you don't have to do that!

317
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:56,620
Isn't going back and forth a-

318
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:58,300
Don't worry, it's not far.

319
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:11,100
It's almost like he was trying to run away.

320
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:13,580
Then you think so too, huh?

321
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:18,140
You really must have been uncomfortable.

322
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:21,340
So it's true that he's awkward with women.

323
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:25,660
I wish I hadn't done that to him.

324
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:41,820
I wish I hadn't done that to him.

325
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:10,760
Girls like Akanechi, who have less hair to deal with, can use this kind of pin to tie their hair up simply.

326
00:23:11,420 --> 00:23:19,520
But girls like Miss Runa, who have an unruly massive hair, turn out like this.

327
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:24,320
Girls who have a whole bunch of hair have a hard time putting it up in ponytails.

328
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:28,680
I'm really jelly that you don't have to deal with this, Akane.

329
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,480
But isn't it better to have more?

330
00:23:31,060 --> 00:23:32,160
Nah, not really.

331
00:23:33,980 --> 00:23:36,720
There's no end to a young girl's anxieties.

332
00:23:36,720 --> 00:23:38,220
Ah.

